WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:09.800
I do feel like I have a little secret.

2
00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:14.520
We have this little Estonia here
that is untouched

3
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.960
and no one knows about it.

4
00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:25.160
Yes...

5
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:30.800
There's that feeling of freedom here.

6
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.760
Just drive down the highway,
get somewhere,

7
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.800
then go out
and you're completely alone.

8
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:40.400
It feels good.

9
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.640
But as they say,
to appreciate something,

10
00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:47.120
you have to leave
in order to come back.

11
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.000
Did it make sense?

12
00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:02.520
GENERATION BEYOND BORDERS

13
00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:07.120
BACK TO ESTONIA?

14
00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:12.280
As soon as you fly
over the Estonian forests,

15
00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:16.760
you see this nice, dense forest,
you see grass and greenery,

16
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.840
you feel so good.

17
00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:21.680
Especially when you fly
over Lake Ülemiste

18
00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.760
and land at Tallinn Airport.

19
00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:27.160
Then you move slowly
through the airport

20
00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:30.440
and you think you're in Estonia,
you hear Estonian everywhere.

21
00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:34.160
Everything is like...
it just feels so good.

22
00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:43.320
I think about going back
to Estonia all the time.

23
00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:47.120
Maybe a little too much,
because you can't keep thinking that

24
00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:51.080
maybe you should be somewhere else.
It's just tiring.

25
00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:53.240
But that thought comes up often.

26
00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:59.000
I think America has made me
a much better person.

27
00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:01.680
I'm much more emotionally intelligent.

28
00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:04.200
I've been doing hard work there,

29
00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:08.600
the kind of low-paid toiling that

30
00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:12.840
I probably wouldn't have had to do
in Estonia with a master's degree.

31
00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:15.280
It didn't bother me at the time.

32
00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.880
It just seemed like
a necessary step to survive.

33
00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:23.240
When you're in that survival mindset,

34
00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:26.320
then you just do what needs to be done.

35
00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.080
Nothing bad happened.

36
00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.800
I mean, I've probably had to take

37
00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:33.680
a few steps back, socio-economically.

38
00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.480
But now I've been here so long

39
00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:40.480
that I'm doing pretty well.

40
00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:44.080
Now returning to Estonia
is also questionable

41
00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:48.360
because I would come back here
for some kind of NGO

42
00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:52.440
or cultural worker's salary,
which is considerably lower here, etc.

43
00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:55.280
Not to say I've achieved
the American dream

44
00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.400
or reached the good life, not that.

45
00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:00.080
But I'm doing well enough there.

46
00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.680
I see my friends in Estonia
complaining about

47
00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:04.680
how hard it is to run a business,

48
00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:07.000
how hard it is
to get funding for projects,

49
00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.840
or to earn a living wage.

50
00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:14.120
Then I inevitably have to think about

51
00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:18.560
whether it is necessary to dismantle,
to level the small success

52
00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:20.880
I have achieved in America,

53
00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:22.760
in order to come back here

54
00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:25.160
for some emotional
and nostalgic reasons.

55
00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:33.960
I definitely think that I would be

56
00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:38.560
welcomed back to Estonia with my
skills, knowledge and experience,

57
00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:42.400
especially those I gained
in Switzerland.

58
00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:46.840
Another question is,
would I be valued?

59
00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:52.480
Rather... rather not.

60
00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:54.920
Unfortunately.

61
00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:59.280
I don't know where things went wrong,

62
00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:04.960
but it's relatively difficult
to survive on Estonian wages,

63
00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:10.000
unless you're an entrepreneur.

64
00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:13.760
This aspect is different
in Switzerland.

65
00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:18.400
In Switzerland you can live a very
good life with a simple paid job.

66
00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:25.200
I feel that I am welcomed
back to Estonia

67
00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:28.040
more as I was when I left.

68
00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:35.360
I think the changes
in my character and values

69
00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:39.920
will make it difficult
for me to return.

70
00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:45.760
I think that mainstream Estonians
or Estonia rather expects me

71
00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:51.160
as an obedient, loyal citizen
of a consumer society.

72
00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:54.680
They don't want someone
who maybe criticizes too much

73
00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:59.280
or disagrees with the decisions
of the state or government,

74
00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.160
or doesn't consume as much
or follow the same principles.

75
00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:11.600
Under what conditions
would I return to Estonia?

76
00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.600
A very difficult question for me.

77
00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:17.440
I don't know what would have
to happen for me to go back.

78
00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:19.920
I really can't imagine.

79
00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:23.440
I feel like all the negative things
that make people go back

80
00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:25.920
have already happened to me,

81
00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:28.920
people have died, gotten sick,
whatever.

82
00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:31.080
Positive things have happened too,

83
00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:33.480
people getting married, having kids,

84
00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.240
getting promotions,

85
00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:38.000
getting some fancy college degrees,

86
00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:40.560
and I still haven't gone back.

87
00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:44.600
I can't imagine.
I can't answer that,

88
00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:47.800
I just don't know
what would have to happen.

89
00:05:55.600 --> 00:06:01.480
We went back to Estonia because
it felt like the right decision.

90
00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:03.800
We had agreed that

91
00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:06.840
we would go back in two years,
and so we did.

92
00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:10.800
But for some reason, which is
extremely difficult to explain,

93
00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:18.760
we no longer felt
comfortable there, at home.

94
00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:25.040
It was...
- A shock.

95
00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:28.120
In a way, it was a shock
or a surprise that...

96
00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:30.160
We didn't expect.
- Absolutely.

97
00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:34.080
We hadn't thought about it at all.
Yeah, we didn't expect it.

98
00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:41.200
And the fact that we no longer
fit into that environment

99
00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:46.880
made us think that
we should leave again.

100
00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:52.200
We were in a kind of mourning state.

101
00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:56.600
I cried for England, I missed England

102
00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:59.040
and wanted to go back there,

103
00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:05.000
I couldn't adapt to
and accept life in Estonia and...

104
00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:07.400
Move on with life there.
- We were somehow...

105
00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:09.440
Stuck.
- Lost. Or I don't know.

106
00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:14.960
Yes. Lost.
- Lost, yeah.

107
00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:29.160
I was at a scholarship interview
in the UK.

108
00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:32.920
It was a very traditional
and large organization.

109
00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:36.520
They asked me,
where do I see myself in 15 years?

110
00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:40.840
I looked at them and said, "in a bog".

111
00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:44.240
Actually, I meant that
this is a place where you can be

112
00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:47.160
completely isolated
from the rest of the world.

113
00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:52.720
Of course, I added the why and the how.

114
00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:56.880
I'm interested in information
technology and entrepreneurship.

115
00:07:56.960 --> 00:07:59.760
It could be close to the airport,
so you can travel if necessary

116
00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:01.680
and have internet access.

117
00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:08.160
But just having the opportunity to be
separate from the rest of the world,

118
00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:10.480
to recharge your batteries on your own.

119
00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:14.600
This is a great value in Estonia,

120
00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:20.520
which I haven't really experienced
to this extent in other countries.

121
00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:29.840
Since my partner is from Lithuania,

122
00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:36.480
our dream is to come back
close to home.

123
00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:45.040
Currently, that dream place
is Estonia and Saaremaa.

124
00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:49.240
Among the fields where I grew up.

125
00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:54.720
To build our own house
and also a restaurant,

126
00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:58.360
which is now possible

127
00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:04.760
thanks to the capital earned
in Dubai and the savings

128
00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:12.160
that help make it all happen.

129
00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:25.880
Do I expect the Estonian state to
do something to move my family back?

130
00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:31.200
The answer is no, the Estonian state
doesn't have to do anything.

131
00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:35.760
Because I don't want to
move back to Estonia.

132
00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:41.640
I've worked so hard to create
my own environment here.

133
00:09:41.800 --> 00:09:45.480
At least, I could say that,

134
00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:51.200
being of active, working age,

135
00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:55.000
nothing is calling me back to Estonia.

136
00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:59.840
Everything will change
when I no longer have to work.

137
00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:03.120
Or rather, when I don't want to work.

138
00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:08.440
Then I can make my decisions
much more easily.

139
00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:13.000
Probably when I go back,

140
00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:18.120
it will be when I'm retired.

141
00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:24.320
I'll probably go to Hiiumaa,

142
00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:28.360
although then I'll have to find
a compromise with my wife,

143
00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:30.680
because she's from Võru.

144
00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:38.200
But I don't expect anyone to do
anything to create the conditions.

145
00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:42.760
I don't need a bigger house,
I don't need a more comfortable life.

146
00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:46.200
I need an interesting life.

147
00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:48.160
GENERATION BEYOND BORDERS

148
00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:52.920
BACK TO ESTONIA?

149
00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:15.520
Translated by Piret Õunapuu
Film Tower
